Nick applies only to roles that genuinely fit and parks the rest, even when the artefacts are fully worked up. He optimises for fit and throughput on winnable roles, not application volume.

Observed parking triggers (2026-06-16 Seek batch of 9):
- **Requires a credential he lacks.** Engineering Manager roles demand formal line-management of engineers, his weakest credential. An EM role is NOT a "safe engineering bridge" — it is people-management, which he does not have formal tenure in.
- **Not product-leaning.** He prefers product work. Pure management or developer-experience roles get parked.
- **Location and recency.** Sydney roles and postings older than ~3-4 weeks get parked. He is Melbourne-based and weights recency.
- **Design-leaning.** Design is not his strength (parked DXC partly for this).
- **Stack mismatch.** Heavy Svelte / Java-React when his core is TS/Node + AI plus Java backend (parked Easygo partly for this).

**Why:** he wants every application to be a real shot, and his time spent on roles where he is genuinely competitive.

**How to apply:** when ranking or triaging a job batch for Nick, weight fit-to-his-actual-credentials and product-leaning over crude lane-bucketing (do not auto-rank "engineering" roles above "product" roles). Never rank EM/management roles as safe bridges. Lead candidates are eng+AI roles and technical-PM/PO roles that reward his eng+product blend, in Melbourne, recently posted. Present a recommended order and expect him to prune it hard. Positioning rules for the artefacts themselves live in `PAI/USER/PROJECTS/career-pivot.md` settled decisions. See also [[feedback-cover-letter-voice]] and [[gotcha-word-pdf-ligature-ats]].
